<title>USA: CKF Bancorp to buy back 5 pct of outstanding stock.</title>
<headline>CKF Bancorp to buy back 5 pct of outstanding stock.</headline>
<dateline>DANVILLE, Ky 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The parent company of Central Kentucky Federal Savings Bank said Wednesday it planned to buy back up to 47,500 shares, which represents five percent of its outstanding common stock.</p>
<p>The company, called CKF Bancorp Inc, said its Incentive Plan Trust would buy the shares in order to give them to holders of stock options.</p>
</text>
